# area: Agent safety
mission AgentSpendBudget

goal
  Admit an agent step only when its reserved cost fits the remaining budget.

why
  Repeated model and tool calls need a predictable spending boundary.

guarantee a proposed charge stays inside the remaining budget
  verify test SpendAdmission

never admit negative cost or negative remaining budget
  verify test SpendAdmission

decision SpendAdmission
  inputs
    remainingCents
    reservedCents
  rule affordable step
    when remainingCents >= 0 and reservedCents >= 0 and reservedCents <= remainingCents
    return Admit
  default
    return Stop

test SpendAdmission
  case below the budget
    given remainingCents 100, reservedCents 99
    expect Admit
  case exactly at the budget
    given remainingCents 100, reservedCents 100
    expect Admit
  case above the budget
    given remainingCents 100, reservedCents 101
    expect Stop
  case exhausted budget
    given remainingCents 0, reservedCents 1
    expect Stop
  case negative reservation
    given remainingCents 100, reservedCents -1
    expect Stop
  case negative budget
    given remainingCents -1, reservedCents 0
    expect Stop

note engineering
  The host must validate integer cents, reserve atomically across concurrent calls, and reconcile actual cost. These cases test admission only.
